# Build context exclusions.
#
# Keep this file in sync with the Dockerfile. It previously excluded
# `bgutil-ytdlp-pot-provider` outright while the Dockerfile still ran
# `cd bgutil-ytdlp-pot-provider/server && npm ci`, so the build failed on a
# missing directory and Render kept serving the last image that happened to
# build. That mismatch is the reason deploys appeared to succeed locally and
# never took effect in production.

# Installed inside the image for the correct platform. Copying a
# Windows-built tree in would break every native module.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Compiled output is produced by the build stage.
dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime scratch space.
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep

# Windows-only binaries are useless in a Linux image and cost ~36MB of build
# context. yt-dlp and ffmpeg come from the Dockerfile instead.
bin/*.exe
bin/*.exe.old

# Secrets are supplied as environment variables by Render, never baked into a
# layer. `.env.example` is documentation and safe to keep.
*.env
.env*
!.env.example

# WireGuard config carrying a private key. Never belongs in an image.
warp.conf

# Local-only scratch and docs.
npm-debug.log*
*.md
.git
.github
.vscode
test-*.js
